# 043 = deployment-local fix for the nightly "no MCP tool registered" cron tick.
#   Not upstream (yet): the stripping predicate below looks like an upstream regression
#   introduced with the per-scope MCP overlay; file an upstream issue before retiring.
#
# Why: every scheduled tick since the v0.22.7 upgrade runs without
#   mcp__chrome_devtools__* while the same gateway PID serves 33 tools to interactive
#   sessions. Log signature (agent.log, every 00:30/06:00 tick):
#     cron.scheduler_mcp: MCP scope=/opt/data configured=1 (chrome-devtools) not_connected=-
#     cron.scheduler_mcp: MCP recovery deadline reached: chrome-devtools
#     cron.scheduler_mcp: no MCP tool registered for this run ... -- scheduled tools stay off
#   No "MCP revival 'chrome-devtools' -> ..." line appears: 041's revival never runs.
#
#   Root cause, two independent defects that reinforce each other:
#   1. mcp_servers_ready() only checks that a server OBJECT exists for the scope. A stdio
#      session recycled by idle_timeout_seconds (900s) still passes it (no connect error,
#      no park). 041 gates _revive_one() on that set, so the dormant server is never
#      re-woken; wait_for_recovery() then waits out the full 15s and returns zero tools.
#   2. discover_mcp_tools() calls register_connected_into_current_scope() first. Its stale
#      sweep treats "session is None" as a dead connection and silently deregisters that
#      scope's MCP tool entries -- but a recycled stdio server is intentionally dormant and
#      its check_fn still advertises the tools (_make_check_fn treats _is_recycled_stdio()
#      as connected). The entries are dropped, then the revival path cannot re-publish them:
#      reconnect keeps _registered_tool_names non-empty and deliberately skips registration.
#
# What it does:
#   * mcp_tool_registration: a recycled stdio connection is not stale -- keep the scope's
#     tool registrations until the session is re-woken or the server actually parks/fails.
#     Config removal/disable and route/credential mismatches still strip, unchanged.
#   * scheduler_mcp: gate the revival set on the same _registered_and_ready() predicate
#     wait_for_recovery() uses, so a dormant or overlay-less server is actually revived.
#   * scheduler_mcp: _ensure_registered() re-publishes this scope's entries after a wake
#     when they are missing (idempotent; a healthy registration returns False).
#
# Verified on v0.23.4 (see commands in the delivery report): patch -p1 --dry-run and real
#   apply rc=0 on a pristine copy of both targets, reverse dry-run rc=0, zero fuzz/.rej/.orig,
#   py_compile clean, and a fake-server unit check of _ensure_registered (missing entries ->
#   re-register once; healthy entries -> no-op).
# Runtime files only: cron/scheduler_mcp.py, tools/mcp_tool_registration.py
# Retire when the upstream fix lands and HERMES_AGENT_VERSION is bumped.

--- a/tools/mcp_tool_registration.py
